  "d9.s1": "① The CPU puts command and data buffers in memory.",
  "d9.s2": "② The CPU writes the doorbell in the device’s BAR. The write crosses the root complex and reaches the device as a memory-write TLP.",
  "d9.s3": "③ The device sends read and write TLPs itself to move data (DMA). The IOMMU translates its addresses into physical ones and stops out-of-range access.",
  "d9.s4": "④ When done, the device sends a memory write to an address starting with FEE, with the interrupt vector as its data. This is MSI.",
  "d9.s5": "⑤ The root complex passes the write to the interrupt controller, which interrupts the CPU to check the result.",
  "d9.aria": "Schematic: CPU, memory, interrupt controller, root complex with IOMMU, and device, with five steps: place the command, ring the doorbell, DMA, MSI write, notify the CPU",
  "d9.cap": "Figure 9 · A device doing a job: doorbell, then DMA, then a memory write to report completion.",
